Author: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Description: Keep the terminal fd non-blocking.
 ply_terminal_open() opens the tty O_NONBLOCK, then makes it blocking. The
 readers poll before they read, but if the input is gone by the time read()
 runs, the read blocks the event loop. PID 1 then blocks writing
 /dev/console into plymouth's full pty, and boot hangs after switch-root
 until a key is pressed. Leave the fd non-blocking and write through a loop
 that waits on EAGAIN while the terminal drains, giving up after a second
 without progress.
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1145446
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-10

--- a/src/libply-splash-core/ply-terminal.c
+++ b/src/libply-splash-core/ply-terminal.c
